{#
    Where the page sits, said as a trail.

    **The element, addressed.** A template that builds the trail itself —
    `sds-nav-breadcrumb`, `sds-crumbs__sep`, `sds-crumbs__here` — is a whole
    component written out in a file that is not the component. What the
    renderer knows is the rootline. Everything after that is the trail's own.

    The separator is a character rather than a glyph and no screen reader
    says it. The last entry is the page and carries `aria-current` instead of
    a link. And the trail spends no accent on where the reader already is.
    Each of those stands once, in `src/components/crumbs.ts`, and this hands
    over the list.

    The last entry keeps no `href` on purpose, and the element drops one
    anyway. A trail whose last step is a link is a trail pasted from the one
    above it.
#}
{%- if rootline|length > 1 -%}
    {%- set items = [] -%}
    {%- for entry in rootline -%}
        {%- set items = items|merge([
            entry.current
                ? { label: entry.value.toString }
                : { label: entry.value.toString, href: renderLink(entry.url) }
        ]) -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    <sds-nav-breadcrumb items="{{ items|json_encode }}"></sds-nav-breadcrumb>
{%- endif -%}
